The duct-tape kernel headers gain their arm64 build shims (aarch64 port, task A4)

Taken from darling PR 1753 darlingserver 0217769, duct-tape/xnu rebased one level up:
arm cpu_data/locks/simple_lock/thread grow the fields and stubs the VMAPPLE arm64
config compiles against, waitq/vm_map/libsa lose x86-only assumptions, and the
VMAPPLE pexpert header stops requiring a real Apple interrupt controller.

